  "body": {
    "storage": {
      "value": "<ac:layout><ac:layout-section ac:type=\"two_right_sidebar\"><ac:layout-cell><h2>About The feature</h2><p><span>The weekly summary view is a summary of the week&rsquo;s load for each service.&nbsp;</span></p><h2>Used By</h2><p><span>Can be used by anyone who is involved in scheduling appointments and managing Patient loads. This hopes to serve as a summary snapshot of the scheduled load of patients. Based on this users can choose to schedule more appointments or not.&nbsp;</span></p><h2>How is it used</h2><ol><li>This View is the default landing page when the user accesses the appointment scheduling module. This view can be accessed anytime by clicking on the &quot;Summary&quot; Tab</li><li>The current week is displayed by default, with the current day highlighted.&nbsp;</li><li>Users can also use the date picker to select a week they choose to view. And can navigate to previous and next weeks.</li><li>Clicking on the count (blue) will take the user to a list of appointments filtered for that day and service in the <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"List View of Appointments\" ri:version-at-save=\"4\" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[list view]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link>.</li><li>The missed appointments are shown in red. It cannot be clicked on.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><br /></p><p><ac:image ac:border=\"true\" ac:height=\"317\" ac:width=\"929\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"weekly-summary.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image></p><p><br /></p></ac:layout-cell><ac:layout-cell><p class=\"auto-cursor-target\"><br /></p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"panel\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"b990fe84-d166-442d-b1c9-a408bacfcd95\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"title\">On This Page</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"toc\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"c7b7632d-e378-4c81-9d5f-ebaeced77f3d\" /></p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p class=\"auto-cursor-target\"><br /></p></ac:layout-cell></ac:layout-section></ac:layout>",
      "representation": "storage",
